{
  "spec": "AIPAY-LEDGER-BALANCES-V1, AIPAY-LEDGER-TRIAL-BALANCE-V1, AIPAY-LEDGER-CHECKPOINT-V1",
  "description": "Ledger checkpoint formats (docs design/ledger-service.md). str and bytes carry a u32 big-endian length, integers are 8-byte big-endian (two's complement for signed values), domain tags have no length prefix. balances digest = SHA-256(\"AIPAY-LEDGER-BALANCES-V1\" || u64 seq || u64 count || (str account_code || i64 units || i64 usd_micros)* ordered by account code bytes), with debit-minus-credit totals. trial balance digest = SHA-256(\"AIPAY-LEDGER-TRIAL-BALANCE-V1\" || str period_id || u64 count || (str gl_code || str dimension_key || str currency || opening, debit, credit, closing units, then opening, debit, credit, closing USD micros as i64)* ordered by gl_code, dimension_key, currency bytes). Merkle roots follow RFC 6962 (leaf prefix 0x00, node prefix 0x01, split at the largest power of two below the count, SHA-256 of the empty string for no leaves). checkpoint digest = SHA-256(\"AIPAY-LEDGER-CHECKPOINT-V1\" || u64 id || str kind || u64 from_seq || u64 to_seq || bytes head_hash || bytes merkle_root || bytes balances_digest || bytes trial_balance_digest || str business_date || str period_id || bytes prev_checkpoint_digest); the signature is ASN.1 DER ECDSA P-256 over that digest; key_id is not signed. Integers are decimal strings; bytes are lowercase hex; input fields are the exact digest inputs. The checkpoints cover the genesis_chain of ledger_canonical_v1.json; every invalid checkpoint must be rejected.",
